From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: program dual-VLAN transactions

Provide verified S/C VLAN translation, VSI/L3 binding and port-role
primitives. Reserve disjoint bridge, VLAN and fallback resources,
prepare actions before publishing keys and verify withdrawals before
releasing dependencies. Flowtable ownership is introduced by the later
lifecycle patch.

Fold the earlier explicit VID zero match into the dual-tag transaction
implementation. Preserve priority-tagged VID zero and the combined
untagged/priority-tagged PVID match for both tag roles.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_bridge.c
@@ -224,7 +224,7 @@ static int ppe_bridge_vsi_get(struct ppe
 	if (vsi >= 0)
 		return vsi;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(pb->vsis) - PPE_L3_VLAN_UPLINKS; i++) {
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(pb->vsis) - PPE_L3_RESERVED_VSIS; i++) {
 		if (pb->vsis[i].br || pb->vsis[i].poisoned)
 			continue;
 
@@ -358,14 +358,15 @@ static int ppe_bridge_vsi_xlt_update(str
 		if (idx < 0) {
 			idx = find_first_zero_bit(pb->xlt_used,
 						  PPE_XLT_RULE_TBL_ENTRIES -
-						  PPE_L3_VLAN_UPLINKS);
+						  PPE_L3_RESERVED_VSIS);
 			if (idx >= PPE_XLT_RULE_TBL_ENTRIES -
-				   PPE_L3_VLAN_UPLINKS)
+				   PPE_L3_RESERVED_VSIS)
 				return -ENOSPC;
 		}
 
 		ret = ppe_ing_xlt_rule_set(pb->ppe_dev, idx, rules[i].bitmap,
-					   rules[i].vid, vsi, false);
+					   -1, rules[i].vid, vsi,
+					   false, false);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
